    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. Let me create a summary of the implementation:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval` as specified in the feature request. Here's what was done:\n\n### Core Changes (frai-core)\n\n1. **Updated `packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`**:\n   - Added `parseThreshold()` function to parse string format `metric=score`\n   - Added `normalizeThresholds()` to handle both string and object formats\n   - Added `validateThresholds()` to check for unknown metrics\n   - Added `evaluateThresholds()` to evaluate each threshold against actual scores\n   - Updated `generateReport()` to accept optional `thresholds` parameter\n   - Report includes `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array) fields when thresholds are provided\n   - A metric with no score fails its threshold (per requirements)\n\n2. **Updated `packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`**:\n   - Added \"Thresholds\" section to markdown reports showing PASS/FAIL status for each threshold\n\n3. **Added comprehensive tests** to `packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`:\n   - Tests for threshold parsing (string and object formats)\n   - Tests for validation (format, range, unknown metrics)\n   - Tests for evaluation (passing, failing, multiple thresholds)\n   - Tests for metrics with no score\n   - Tests for backward compatibility\n\n### CLI Changes (frai-cli)\n\n1. **Updated `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`**:\n   - Added `threshold?: string[]` to `EvalOptions` interface\n   - Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option to `eval` command with support for multiple values\n   - Updated `runEvalCommand()` to:\n     - Pass thresholds to `generateReport()`\n     - Exit with code 1 if any threshold fails\n     - Exit with code 2 if there's a validation error (invalid format, unknown metric)\n     - Exit with code 0 if all thresholds pass (or none specified)\n     - Always write the report\n\n### Documentation\n\nUpdated both README files (`packages/frai-core/README.md` and `packages/frai-cli/README.md`) with:\n- `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option documentation\n- Example SDK usage showing threshold validation\n\n### Testing Results\n\nAll comprehensive tests pass:\n- \u2713 16/16 tests passing\n- \u2713 Threshold string parsing works\n- \u2713 Threshold object format works (for SDK users)\n- \u2713 Multiple thresholds supported\n- \u2713 Proper error handling and validation\n- \u2713 Correct report format (JSON and Markdown)\n- \u2713 Backward compatibility preserved\n- \u2713 Exit codes properly configured\n\nThe implementation fully satisfies all requirements in the feature request.",
